  "limits": [
    "Curve API only, with 2 to 64 paired stations including both source endpoints at output 0 and 1, and at most 4096 fitted controls. Stations must increase together after sorting. Degenerate normalized distances/knots or a global interpolant without positive derivative controls reject; there is no automatic monotone fallback.",
    "Position constraints have exact rational stored-curve distance bounds at absolute numerical tolerance. General source-to-fitted-curve error remains adaptive sampled fitting; no continuous source-to-fit image certificate is claimed.",
    "Cubic fitted curves are C2 away from retained source corners. A later Gordon surface has separate continuity requirements. Original source geometry remains unchanged.",
    "Each diagnostic Gordon candidate admits complete images of its supplied curves at 1e-6. For refitted inputs this proves fitted images, not a separate continuous bound against pre-fit originals.",
    "The diagnostic compares returned closest-point outputs on one retained fixture; it is not a continuous surface separation/Hausdorff proof or a broader Rhino qualification. Saved tensor parameter traces are sampled Rust closest-point queries, not proofs of exact isoparametric containment.",
    "Arc-length refitting improves this single fixture comparison; the tested global smooth map worsens it. Neither passes the 1e-6 point-output comparison. NetworkSrf remains unregistered and its surface fitting policy, continuity, complete original-curve admission and broader comparisons remain unfinished.",
    "SMLib, SM_API and adapter archives are instrumented by AddressSanitizer. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented; leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled."
  ],
